# Shell scripts and control fixtures must arrive with LF on every platform.
#
# 🔴 Measured 2026-08-15 on a real windows-latest runner: without this, Git for
# Windows checks files out with CRLF, and `MATCH some string\r` stops matching
# the hook's output. Every EXPECT in attention-anchor.cases failed while the
# guards passed — because the guards only test empty-versus-non-empty output and
# never compare a string, so they survived the same corruption unnoticed.
#
# The dependency gates all passed on that run. It was never a missing tool.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh     text eol=lf
*.cases  text eol=lf
*.mjs    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf

*.png binary
